  note = {The '20X' figure is the document's own headline (title and body text: 'deliver up to 20X speedup in inference throughput'), a release-over-release comparison shown in an image figure rather than broken out per model size in the text. The document's separate FlexGen-comparison table covers exactly five models: OPT-30B, OPT-66B, OPT-175B, BLOOM-176B, and LLaMA2-70B (not OPT-6.7B/13B, and not an 'OPT-176B' model, which does not exist -- 176B is BLOOM's size). FlexGen is marked 'Unsupported' for BLOOM-176B and LLaMA2-70B in that table, so only OPT-30B/66B/175B have a direct head-to-head figure; on those three, ZeRO-Inference's best configuration exceeds FlexGen's best configuration (22.74 vs 21.97 on OPT-30B; 8.08 vs 6.24 on OPT-66B; 2.26 vs 1.84 on OPT-175B).}
